/code-review high — loop U4, round 3, range 31fcdb7..71fcfa5

I found 10 problems on branch `2026-10-21-packs-and-base-split`. The most serious is a change in mise load order. Each repository's `_repo` folder can no longer override the settings that used to sit in `_base`, because the new tool folders sort after `_repo` and mise gives later folders priority.

What I checked:
- `mise run test:repo-sync` passes all 9 cases.
- I also ran the sync myself against scratch consumer repositories. That is how I confirmed the generated mise files, the new pre-commit hook order and the `default_envs = []` case.
- The mise docs (via Context7) confirm the load order: folders under `conf.d` load alphabetically and later ones win.

I left out three things on purpose:
- The docs and this repository's own `.config/bootstrap.toml` (still `tools = [ "base" ]`) are not updated yet. The plan has units U5 (docs) and U6 (this repository's values file and synced copies) for that, and both are still pending. I flag the missing docs only as a CLAUDE.md rule break (finding 8).
- Existing consumers break because their `setup/configs/sync` still loads the old `tools/base/` path. I skipped this because your standing rule is no upgrade paths for old setup files.

